# Mobile-first

Hard requirement. See blueprint §10.1. Build the phone layout first.

- Unprefixed Tailwind classes are the phone layout. Use `sm:`, `md:`, and `lg:` only to add space, columns, or a sidebar.
- Do not build the phone layout with `max-*` overrides of a desktop layout.
- One column on a phone. A second column starts at `md`.
- Primary actions stay in thumb reach. Tap targets are at least 44px. Do not require hover.
- Phone shell uses bottom tabs (Home, Calendar, Directory, Inbox, More). From `md` up, those same links are a sidebar and the tab bar is hidden.
- Pad for the tab bar and `env(safe-area-inset-*)`.
- Check a phone-width viewport before finishing a UI change, and `md` when a wider layout was added.
